<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan buys 450,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Pakistan buys 450,000 tonnes U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan awarded eight contracts for 450,000 tonnes of U.S. soft white wheat on Monday, with prices ranging from $152.48 to $155.56 per tonne FOB, a Food and Agriculture Ministry official said.  </p>
<p>He said the wheat was for delivery between March 10 to 31.</p>
<p>The contracts were awarded to the following trading firms:</p>
<p>    Tradigrain					    50,000 tonnes</p>
<p>    Kanematsu					     15,000</p>
<p>    CGII						    85,000</p>
<p>    HSC						     40,000</p>
<p>    Continental					   85,000</p>
<p>    UGC						     60,000</p>
<p>    Cargill						100,000</p>
<p>    LDC						     15,000</p>
<p>    -----						  -------</p>
<p>    TOTAL						  450,000</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
